// Open DevTools: Right-click your page, select Inspect, and click the Sources tab.Find Your Script: Open your JavaScript file from the left sidebar.Set a Breakpoint: Click on the line number next to console.log(prettyJson);. A blue or red marker will appear.Trigger the Code: Refresh your browser page. The script will freeze execution exactly at that line.Check the Values:Scope Panel: Look at the Scope window on the right side of DevTools. Under "Local", you will see both variables.Hovering: Hover your mouse cursor directly over the words standardJson and prettyJson in your code editor line.What you will see: standardJson looks like a dense string block, while prettyJson displays with line breaks (\n) and readable spaces.